,"_gate_roic_consistency":null,"_gp_roic_consistency":null,"_score_roic_consistency":null,"_gate_incr_roic":null,"_gp_incr_roic":null,"_score_incr_roic":null,"_gate_margin_advantage":null,"_gp_margin_advantage":null,"_score_margin_advantage":null,"_gate_pool_share":-0.3243465750605171,"_gp_pool_share":false,"_score_pool_share":0.0,"_gate_rev_durability":null,"_gp_rev_durability":null,"_score_rev_durability":0.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":null,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":null,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":null,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.02136712066681944,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":34.9,"_gate_share_shrink":-0.07200288188902693,"_gp_share_shrink":true,"_score_share_shrink":100.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":1.8017207081758504,"_gp_sbc_dilution":false,"_score_sbc_dilution":0.0,"_gate_insider_own":0.3451,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":100.0,"_gate_insider_buying":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"PennyMac Financial Services, Inc., through its subsidiaries, engages in the mortgage banking and investment management activities in the United States. The company operates through two segments, Production and Servicing. The Production segment is involved in the origination, acquisition, and sale of loans. This segment also sources residential conventional and government-insured or guaranteed mortgage loans through correspondent production, consumer direct lending, and broker direct lending. The Servicing segment performs loan administration, collection, and default management activities, including the collection and remittance of loan payments; responds to customer inquiries; provides accounting for principal and interest; holds custodial funds for the payment of property taxes and insurance premiums; offers counseling for delinquent borrowers; and supervising foreclosures and property dispositions, as well as administers loss mitigation activities comprising modification and forbearance programs, and supervising foreclosures and property dispositions. The company was founded in 2008 and is headquartered in Westlake Village, California.","ceo_bio":"Mr. David A. Spector | CEO & Chairman | Age 62 | Compensation: $5.2M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 5K people. Revenue per employee of $4K ranks in the bottom quartile among Financial Services peers, with revenue falling 43%/yr across its filed history. Stock-based compensation of $7K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 1296\u00d7 revenue per employee (very high relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (6/10).","financial_summary":["PennyMac Financial Services, In is a mid-cap financial services business with a $3.1B market cap on $20M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +18% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at 5% against a 11% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The company is burning through $1.7B of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 10.3\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and thin 0.6\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield of 2.1% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and stock-based comp at 180% of revenue is silent dilution an owner has to account for, and insiders hold 35% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is, and within its sector the business captures 105.7\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotroski score 2/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.3) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Accruals running hot at +7.3% of assets \u2014 earnings quality bears watching","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Elevated short interest (13.0% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting the other way","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Significant insider selling (net $2.5M)","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","dollars":-2493706.83},{"text":"Value-trap profile (score 54/100): leveraged balance sheet under pressure; roic below cost of capital \u2014 cheapness may reflect deterioration, not mispricing","sev":"amber","cat":"value_trap"},{"text":"Carries more leverage than most Financial Services peers \u2014 a smaller cushion for the inevitable bad year","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 2713% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Trading at a 47% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Responsive Playbooks and the PFSI Inflection","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_r